This directory contains example scripts and the resulting outputs
discussed in the papers submitted to CPC. Two versions of the scripts
are present, one is for Python interface (*.py), and the other is for
SFAC interface (*.sf).

structure/,  atomic structure example for Ne-like Fe.
excitation/, electron impact excitation example for Ne-like Fe.
pirr/,       photoionzation and radiative recombination for Li-like Fe.
aidr/,       autoionization example for Ne-like Se.
ionization/, electron impact ionization example for Ne-like Fe.
NeL/.        a simple collisional-radiative model example for NeVIII.
FeL/,        a general application to the calculation of Fe-L shell
	     spectrum of collisionally ionized plasma. It includes
	     the recombination, and ionization processes in the
	     line formation.
polariz/,    use of pfac.pol module to calculate the polarizations of
	     He-like Fe lines.
rmatrix/,    collisional excitation with the Dirac R-matrix method.

These scripts are also used to check the healthy state of the code.
`ref` in each example contains the reference results by FAC=1.1.4.

Testing
=======

`check.py` is the single entry point for running the demos and for
comparing their output against `ref/`. It needs pfac to be importable
(e.g. `pip install .`, or after `meson install` with the install prefix on
PYTHONPATH).

    python check.py

runs every demo that has reference data and then checks it, stopping at
the first failure. Useful variations:

    python check.py -l                 list demos, scripts and results
    python check.py -c                 only compare existing output vs ref/
    python check.py structure NeL      restrict to a couple of demos
    python check.py -j8                run up to 8 demos at once
    python check.py --openmp           run with OpenMP (run only, see below)
    python check.py -C                 remove generated demo output
    python check.py -R tests           re-baseline demo/tests/ref
    python check.py -k                 keep going after a failing demo
    python check.py -v                 show each script and file checked

`FeL` and `rmatrix` produce no reference data and are slow, so they are
not part of the default set: name them explicitly, or pass `--all`.

OpenMP runs group levels into blocks in a different order and with different
`IBLK`/`FBLK` group labels than serial runs, so their output cannot be
compared against the serial data in `ref/`. `--openmp` therefore only runs the
demos; `-c` still compares if you ask for it explicitly.

Note that `-R` copies the freshly written files verbatim, so the `TSess`
line at the top of every result (the session timestamp) changes too. Keep
the `ref/` diff limited to the numbers you actually meant to update.

Adding a demo
=============

Add an entry to the `DEMOS` table at the bottom of `check.py` listing its
`scripts` (run in order, with the demo directory as cwd), the `results`
that are compared against `ref/` and refreshed by `-R`, and the `outputs`
that `-C` deletes. Files that are produced but have no comparator can be
listed under `unchecked` so `-l` mentions them.
